  "body": [
    "American nuclear power companies increased their purchases of Russian uranium enrichment services in 2025, the first full calendar year following the enactment of a federal ban on Russian enriched uranium imports.",
    "The increase occurred as Washington committed billions of dollars toward rebuilding America's domestic nuclear fuel industry.",
    "According to the U.S. Energy Information Administration, American nuclear power operators purchased 3.284 million separative work units of Russian enrichment services in 2025, up from 3.043 million in 2024.",
    "That represents an increase of approximately 7.9%.",
    "Russia's share of American enrichment purchases climbed from 20.1% to 25.8%, even as total U.S. purchases declined by more than 16%.",
    "American-origin enrichment purchases increased only slightly, from 2.892 million to 2.930 million separative work units.",
    "The figures measure enrichment services purchased by nuclear operators, rather than the physical weight of uranium imported. They nevertheless reveal the scale of America's continuing reliance on Russian enrichment.",
    "The American company relying on Russia",
    "At the center of Washington's effort to rebuild domestic enrichment capacity is Centrus Energy, an American nuclear fuel supplier with operations in Ohio and Tennessee.",
    "On June 30, 2026, a Centrus subsidiary signed a $900 million contract with the Department of Energy to establish commercial-scale production capacity for high-assay low-enriched uranium, known as HALEU, in Piketon, Ohio.",
    "The agreement provides for payments tied to project milestones, according to the company's SEC filing.",
    "But Centrus remains heavily dependent on TENEX, a subsidiary of Russia's state-owned nuclear corporation Rosatom.",
    "In its November 5 quarterly filing, Centrus disclosed that substantially more than half of the low-enriched uranium it expects to deliver through 2027 was sourced under its TENEX contract.",
    "The company acknowledged that its alternative suppliers cannot fully replace those Russian supplies.",
    "The American company helping Washington reduce its dependence on Russian enrichment is therefore managing that same dependence within its existing commercial operations.",
    "Two deadlines that do not align",
    "The United States enacted its prohibition on Russian low-enriched uranium imports in May 2024, citing energy and national security concerns.",
    "Congress included temporary exemptions allowing the Department of Energy to authorize imports when alternative supplies were unavailable or when continued imports served the national interest.",
    "Under the federal waiver rules, those exemptions must terminate no later than January 1, 2028.",
    "Centrus, however, stated in its July 1 expansion announcement that its first new enrichment capacity is expected to begin operating by 2029.",
    "That leaves a potential gap between the expiration of Russian import waivers and the arrival of new Centrus production capacity.",
    "The Government Accountability Office has independently identified the possibility of a near-term enrichment supply shortage as Russian imports are phased out and demand increases.",
    "Its 2026 nuclear fuel report also documented the waivers granted to Centrus for committed deliveries through 2027.",
    "The timing problem extends beyond one company. Reuters reported on September 18 that American officials were pressing enrichment suppliers to accelerate expansion projects to avoid potential fuel shortages.",
    "Moscow retains leverage",
    "The continuing relationship provides Russia with more than commercial revenue.",
    "In November 2024, Moscow restricted enriched uranium exports to the United States. Centrus disclosed that the Russian restrictions have been extended through December 2027, requiring TENEX to obtain individual export authorizations for shipments to the company.",
    "Most shipments have continued, according to Centrus, although future Russian approvals are not guaranteed.",
    "That gives Moscow influence over part of the fuel supply chain Washington is attempting to secure.",
    "American utilities benefit from continued access to enrichment services, while Centrus can fulfill existing customer commitments as it builds domestic capacity.",
    "TENEX, meanwhile, retains access to commercial sales during the transition.",
    "The available records do not establish the precise revenue Russia receives from Centrus or show that federal funding awarded to Centrus is being transferred to Russian suppliers.",
    "Rebuilding an industry takes time",
    "There is evidence that the American expansion is progressing.",
    "In its November 4 quarterly results, Centrus reported that it had begun shipping newly manufactured centrifuges from Tennessee, secured contracts with critical suppliers and completed an initial construction design package.",
    "Other enrichment companies, including Urenco and Orano, are also pursuing capacity expansions that could help meet American demand.",
    "The $900 million Centrus contract specifically supports HALEU production, primarily intended for advanced nuclear technologies. It should not be treated as a direct replacement for every unit of conventional low-enriched uranium currently purchased from Russia.",
    "Centrus's broader expansion plans include both fuel types.",
    "Continued Russian purchases under authorized waivers are not evidence of sanctions evasion. The exemptions were deliberately included to protect the country's nuclear fuel supply while alternatives were developed.",
    "But the federal purchasing data show that reducing dependence on Russia has proved more complicated than passing an import ban.",
    "Washington has established a deadline for ending the exemptions. The industry must now demonstrate that sufficient alternative fuel supplies will be available when that deadline arrives."
  ],
